      "knowledge_point": "Describing Properties of the Secant Function",
      "problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x?$\n\nI. The point $(0,2)$ is in the graph\n\nII. $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ is a vertical asymptote\n\nIII. $y=-2$ belongs to the range of the function.",
      "worked_solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=sec⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934039/assets/da729794a0331383debd75be0a4ce4a9f2d4da3286f50bd4f284868996077412.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The $y$-intercept of $sec⁡x$ is $1.$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function $y=sec⁡x$ has asymptotes at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,$ thus $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ is a vertical asymptote.\n\n- Statement III is true. The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ),$ so $y=-2$ belongs to the range.",
